<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Parakeet Café · 2027 Sales Objectives: A Second Look</title>
<style>
{% include "deck_style.css" %}</style>
</head>
<body>
{% set t = n.t %}{% set C = n.C %}
{% macro head(eyebrow) %}<div class="head"><img src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Café"><span class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</span></div>{% endmacro %}
{% macro foot(note) %}<div class="foot"><span>Parakeet Café · 2027 Sales Objectives: A Second Look</span><span>{{ note }}</span><span class="pn"></span></div>{% endmacro %}
{% macro badge(v) %}<span class="badge {{ v }}">{{ VERDICT_LABEL[v] }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% set SRC = "Toast POS net sales through Oct 14, 2026 · budget: “2027 Sales Objectives by Café – Investors”, Oct 2026" %}

{# ================================================================== 1 COVER #}
<section class="page cover">
  <div class="cover-left">
    <img class="logo" src="assets/logo-bird.png" alt="Parakeet Café">
    <div class="eyebrow">Budget review · October 2026</div>
    <div class="cover-title">2027 Sales<br>Objectives:<br>A Second Look</div>
    <p class="cover-sub">The 2026 finish holds up. The 2027 objectives assume our cafés stop growing. What four years of Toast sales say, café by café.</p>
    <div class="cover-meta">
      Reviewing “2027 Sales Objectives by Café – Investors” (prepared by the CFO, October 2026)<br>
      Toast POS net sales, {{ n.first_day.strftime("%B %Y") }} – {{ n.last_day.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") }} · prepared October 15, 2026
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cover-right"><img src="assets/hero-3.jpg" alt=""></div>
</section>

{# ================================================================== 2 SUMMARY #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("The short version") }}
  <h1>2026 holds up. The 2027 objectives assume our cafés stop growing.</h1>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="col flist" style="flex:1.5">
      <div class="finding"><div class="num">01</div><p><b>2026 holds up.</b> The budget's {{ t.b26 | fm }} finish for the nine cafés is within {{ t.d26 | apct }} of ours (Toast to September plus our October–December forecast) and within 2% café by café; {{ "%.0f" | format(t.booked_share * 100) }}% of the year is already booked. The one gap is scope: Nautilus ({{ C["Nautilus"].e26 | fm }}) is not in the budget.</p></div>
      <div class="finding"><div class="num">02</div><p><b>2027 assumes growth stops.</b> {{ t.bg | pct }} is about what the nine cafés would sell if they simply held their September level ({{ t.hold_lo | pct(0) }} to {{ t.hold_hi | pct(0) }}). They are growing {{ t.ytd_g | apct(0) }} this year and {{ t.oct_g | apct(0) }} in October.</p></div>
      <div class="finding"><div class="num">03</div><p><b>Five cafés carry most of the gap.</b> {{ n.strong.names[:-1] | join(", ") }} and {{ n.strong.names[-1] }} are growing {{ n.strong.ytd_lo | apct(0) }}–{{ n.strong.ytd_hi | apct(0) }} this year and are budgeted at {{ n.strong.bg_lo | apct(0) }}–{{ n.strong.bg_hi | apct(0) }}: {{ "%.0f" | format(n.strong.share * 100) }}% of the {{ t.gap | fm(1) }} gap between the budget and our plan.</p></div>
      <div class="finding"><div class="num">04</div><p><b>The budget is bolder than we are on new cafés.</b> Manhattan Beach and Sportsmen's Lodge are budgeted at {{ n.bridge27.new_budget | fm }}, {{ (n.bridge27.new_budget / n.bridge27.new_track - 1) | apct(0) }} more than an average opening of ours would bring ({{ n.bridge27.new_track | fm }}). We would also wait for the Cove remodel to trade before counting it.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="score">
        <div class="slab">2027 net sales · nine existing cafés</div>
        <div class="s budget"><div class="k">Budget</div><div class="v">{{ t.b27 | fm }}</div><div class="g">{{ t.bg | pct }}</div></div>
        <div class="s"><div class="k">What we suggest</div><div class="v">{{ n.suggest.nine | fm }}</div><div class="g">{{ (n.suggest.nine / t.e26 - 1) | pct }}</div></div>
        <div class="s plan"><div class="k">Our plan</div><div class="v">{{ t.plan27 | fm }}</div><div class="g">{{ t.pg | pct }}</div></div>
        <p class="note" style="margin-top:10px">Growth on each one's 2026 finish ({{ t.b26 | fm }} budget, {{ t.e26 | fm }} ours). What we suggest = our plan where the data backs it, the budget where it doesn't. Our plan = three forecasting models, leaning low on purpose.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="strip pin-bottom"><span class="lab">We suggest</span><span><b>{{ n.suggest.total | fm }}</b> for the total company in 2027, {{ n.suggest.total_change | sfm }} above the budget's {{ n.suggest.total_budget | fm }}: raise six café objectives, keep three, add Nautilus, and budget the new cafés on our opening record.</span></div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 3 DIVIDER 1 #}
<section class="page divider">
  <div class="div-left">
    <div class="part">Part 1</div>
    <div class="div-title">The 2026 finish</div>
    <p class="div-sub">With two and a half months to go, how far off can the 2026 estimate be?</p>
    <ul class="div-list">
      <li><span>01</span>{{ "%.0f" | format(t.booked_share * 100) }}% of the year is already booked</li>
      <li><span>02</span>Our forecast for October–December</li>
      <li><span>03</span>Café by café: the budget against our finish</li>
      <li><span>04</span>The only real gap: Nautilus</li>
    </ul>
    <img class="bird" src="assets/parrot-map.png" alt="">
  </div>
  <div class="div-right"><img src="assets/split-order.jpg" alt=""></div>
</section>

{# ================================================================== 4 BOOKED #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 1 · The 2026 finish") }}
  <h1>{{ "%.0f" | format(t.booked_share * 100) }}% of 2026 is already booked, so the estimate can only move so much</h1>
  <p class="lede">Through October 14, Toast has recorded {{ t.booked | fm }} for the nine existing cafés, {{ "%.0f" | format(t.booked_share * 100) }}% of the budget's {{ t.b26 | fm }} finish. The eleven weeks left would have to miss by 5% to move the year by about 1%.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.7">
      <div class="chart-title">2026 net sales by month, nine existing cafés</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">October–December: the budget's estimate (gray) and our forecast (pink marks)</div>
      {{ svg.booked }}
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="stat"><div class="lab">Booked, January 1 – October 14</div><div class="val">{{ t.booked | fm }}</div><div class="cap">{{ "%.0f" | format(t.booked_share * 100) }}% of the budget's 2026 finish</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="lab">Still to come, October 15 – December 31</div><div class="val">{{ t.to_come | fm }}</div><div class="cap">about eleven weeks of trading</div></div>
      <div class="stat pinktop"><div class="lab">If those eleven weeks miss by 5%</div><div class="val">±{{ (t.to_come * 0.05) | fm }}</div><div class="cap">±{{ "%.1f" | format(t.to_come * 0.05 / t.b26 * 100) }}% on the year</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="strip pin-bottom"><span class="lab">How it's estimated</span><span>The budget grows each café's October–December 2025 sales at its own Q3 2026 rate ({{ t.b_q3 | pct }} for the nine on the budget's figures). Our own forecast for the quarter, from the same three models we use for 2027, is on the next page.</span></div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 4b OUR Q4 FORECAST #}
{% set Q = n.q4 %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 1 · The 2026 finish") }}
  <h1>Our own forecast for October–December lands within {{ "%.0f" | format(((Q.ours_total / Q.budget_total - 1) | abs) * 100 + 0.5) }}% of the budget's</h1>
  <p class="lede">We forecast the rest of 2026 with the same three models we use for 2027. For the nine existing cafés they expect {{ Q.ours_total | fm }} in October–December, {{ (Q.ours_total - Q.budget_total) | fk }} ({{ (Q.ours_total / Q.budget_total - 1) | pct }}) {{ "more" if Q.ours_total > Q.budget_total else "less" }} than the budget, and October so far is running slightly ahead of both.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.65">
      <div class="chart-title">October–December 2026 by month, nine existing cafés</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Net sales · whisker: lowest to highest of our three models</div>
      {{ svg.q4 }}
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <table class="roomy">
        <thead><tr><th class="l">Oct–Dec</th><th>Net sales</th><th>vs 2025</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Same months, 2025</td><td>{{ Q.ly_total | fm }}</td><td class="dim">—</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Budget estimate</td><td>{{ Q.budget_total | fm }}</td><td>{{ (Q.budget_total / Q.ly_total - 1) | pct }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>Our forecast</b></td><td class="pink"><b>{{ Q.ours_total | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (Q.ours_total / Q.ly_total - 1) | pct }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="dim">Our three models</td><td class="dim">{{ Q.lo_total | frange(Q.hi_total) }}</td><td class="dim">{{ (Q.lo_total / Q.ly_total - 1) | pct(0) }} to {{ (Q.hi_total / Q.ly_total - 1) | pct(0) }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h3 style="margin-top:22px">October so far (1–14)</h3>
      <div class="minis">
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Actual</div><div class="val">{{ Q.oct_actual | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Our forecast</div><div class="val">{{ Q.oct_ours | fm }}</div><div class="sub">actual {{ (Q.oct_actual / Q.oct_ours - 1) | pct }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Budget's rule</div><div class="val">{{ Q.oct_rule | fm }}</div><div class="sub">actual {{ (Q.oct_actual / Q.oct_rule - 1) | pct }}</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="strip pin-bottom"><span class="lab">2026 finish</span><span>Our forecast makes the nine cafés' 2026 <b>{{ t.e26 | fm }}</b> (Toast to September plus our October–December), against the budget's {{ t.b26 | fm }}: {{ t.d26 | pct }}. If October's pace ({{ t.oct_g | pct }} on last year) held for the quarter, it would add about {{ (t.q4_oct_pace - t.q4_b) | fk }} to the budget's figure.</span></div>
  {{ foot("Our forecast: blend of Prophet, SARIMA and Holt-Winters fitted through Sep 30, 2026 · " ~ SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 5 TABLE #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 1 · The 2026 finish") }}
  <h1>Café by café, the budget's 2026 finish matches ours within 2%</h1>
  <p class="lede">Both start from January–September actuals that agree within 0.1% (the budget's September sales report against Toast) and differ in how October–December is estimated: the budget's Q3-growth rule against our three forecasting models.</p>
  <table class="roomy">
    <thead><tr>
      <th class="l">Café</th><th>Jan–Sep 2026<br>actual</th><th>vs Jan–Sep<br>2025</th><th>Oct–Dec<br>budget</th><th>Oct–Dec<br>our models</th>
      <th>2026 finish<br>budget</th><th>2026 finish<br>ours</th><th>Difference</th><th>Oct 1–14<br>vs 2025</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for s in n.nine %}{% set c = C[s] %}
      <tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ c.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ c.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.q4_b | fk }}</td><td>{{ c.q4_o | fk }}</td>
        <td>{{ c.b26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ c.e26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ c.d26 | pct }}</td><td>{{ c.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
      <tr class="total"><td>Nine existing cafés</td><td>{{ t.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td>{{ t.q4_b | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.q4_o | fm }}</td>
        <td>{{ t.b26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.e26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.d26 | pct }}</td><td>{{ t.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
      {% set cv = C["La Jolla Cove"] %}{% set na = C["Nautilus"] %}
      <tr class="sep"><td class="dim">La Jolla Cove <small>(budget: remodels)</small></td><td class="dim">{{ cv.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.q4_b | fk }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.q4_o | fk }}</td>
        <td class="dim">{{ cv.b26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.e26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.d26 | pct }}</td><td class="dim">{{ cv.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Nautilus <small class="pink">(not in the budget)</small></td><td>{{ na.ytd26 | fm }}</td><td>{{ na.ytd_g | pct }}</td><td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.q4_o | fk }}</td>
        <td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.e26 | fm }}</td><td class="dim">—</td><td>{{ na.oct_g | pct }}</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note pin-bottom">Our finish = January–September Toast actuals + our models' October–December forecast. Budget columns come from the budget workbook; its January–September for Beverly Hills is {{ (C["Beverly Hills"].ytd26 - C["Beverly Hills"].b_ytd) | fk }} below Toast, so the columns do not add across for that café. Del Mar Café appears as Carmel Valley in Toast.</p>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 6 BRIDGE 2026 #}
{% set B = n.bridge26 %}{% set bmax = B.ours %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 1 · The 2026 finish") }}
  <h1>The only real 2026 gap is scope: Nautilus is not in the budget</h1>
  <p class="lede">The budget's total-company 2026 is {{ B.budget_total | fm }}; our finish for all eleven cafés is {{ B.ours | fm }}. {{ "%.0f" | format(B.nautilus / (B.ours - B.budget_total) * 100) }}% of the {{ (B.ours - B.budget_total) | fk }} difference is one café the budget leaves out.</p>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:8px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.5">
      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="r"><div class="what">Budget: nine existing cafés</div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ B.budget9 / bmax * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.budget9 | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ La Jolla Cove<small>in the budget, listed under remodels</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.cove / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%;background:var(--g400)"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.cove | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r tot"><div class="what">= Budget: total company</div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ B.budget_total / bmax * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.budget_total | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ Nautilus<small>trading all year; not in the budget</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.nautilus / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt pink">{{ B.nautilus | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ October–December estimates<small>our models vs the budget's rule, eleven cafés</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ B.diff / bmax * 100 * 8 }}%;background:var(--g400)"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.diff | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r tot final"><div class="what">= Our 2026 finish, all eleven cafés<small>Toast to September + our October–December forecast</small></div><div><div class="bar ours" style="width:100%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ B.ours | fm }}</div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px">Bars for the adjustments are drawn at 8× scale so they are visible next to the totals.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="box">
        <h3>Nautilus</h3>
        <p>Our weekday-only café has traded all year: {{ C["Nautilus"].ytd26 | fm }} in January–September ({{ C["Nautilus"].ytd_g | pct }}) and {{ C["Nautilus"].oct_sales | fk }} in October 1–14 ({{ C["Nautilus"].oct_g | pct }}).</p>
        <p>It appears nowhere in the budget, neither among the existing cafés nor under new and remodeled cafés.</p>
        <p><b>Question for the budget:</b> is Nautilus closing, or reported somewhere else? If not, it adds {{ C["Nautilus"].e26 | fm }} to 2026 and about {{ C["Nautilus"].plan27 | fm }} to 2027.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="strip pin-bottom"><span class="lab">Bottom line</span><span>Excluding Nautilus, the budget's 2026 and ours differ by {{ B.diff | fk }} ({{ "%.1f" | format(B.diff / B.budget_total * 100) }}%). <b>We agree on 2026.</b> The disagreement is about 2027.</span></div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 7 DIVIDER 2 #}
<section class="page divider">
  <div class="div-left">
    <div class="part">Part 2</div>
    <div class="div-title">2027</div>
    <p class="div-sub">The objectives assume our cafés stop growing in January. Their sales say otherwise.</p>
    <ul class="div-list">
      <li><span>01</span>The budget is a no-growth plan</li>
      <li><span>02</span>Every café is growing faster than its objective</li>
      <li><span>03</span>Where the gap sits, and where the budget is bolder</li>
      <li><span>04</span>Total company and what we suggest</li>
    </ul>
    <img class="bird" src="assets/parrot-map.png" alt="">
  </div>
  <div class="div-right"><img src="assets/hero-1.jpg" alt=""></div>
</section>

{# ================================================================== 8 NO-GROWTH #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>The budget's {{ t.bg | pct }} is about what we'd sell if growth stopped today</h1>
  <p class="lede">Holding each of the nine cafés at its September level for all of 2027, with its usual seasonal swings, gives {{ t.hold_lo | pct }} to {{ t.hold_hi | pct }} on 2026 (two estimates). The budget sits in that range. Our plan assumes growth slows to {{ t.pg | apct(0) }}, not to zero.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.75">
      <div class="chart-title">Monthly net sales, nine existing cafés</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">From October 2026: our forecast and the budget's · gray band: no growth after September 2026 (two estimates)</div>
      {{ svg.brand }}
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="chart-title">Same-store growth by year</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">2024–2026E as reported in the budget · 2027 on the same nine cafés</div>
      {{ svg.comp }}
      <div class="callout" style="margin-top:10px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:12px">The cafés added <b>{{ t.added26 | fm(1) }}</b> in 2026. The budget adds <b>{{ t.added27_b | fm(1) }}</b> in 2027; our plan adds <b class="pink">{{ t.added27_p | fm(1) }}</b>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot("No-growth estimates: seasonal run-rate of Jul–Sep 2026 sales; and each café's Prophet trend held at its Sep 30, 2026 level") }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 9 DUMBBELL #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>Every café is growing faster this year than the budget allows for 2027</h1>
  <p class="lede">For all nine cafés, the budget's 2027 growth is below what the café is delivering in 2026. For {{ n.below_slowest | length }} of them it is below the café's slowest quarter on record.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.6">
      <div class="chart-title">Sales growth: 2026 so far against 2027 in the budget and in our plan</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Jan–Sep 2026 vs Jan–Sep 2025 · 2027 vs each one's 2026 finish</div>
      {{ svg.dumbbell }}
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="stat"><div class="lab">Cafés growing faster in 2026 than their 2027 objective</div><div class="val">{{ n.faster_than_budget | length }} of 9</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="lab">Objectives below the café's slowest quarter on record</div><div class="val">{{ n.below_slowest | length }} of 9</div><div class="cap">{{ n.below_slowest | join(", ") }}</div></div>
      <div class="stat pinktop"><div class="lab">Volume, not price: Jan–Sep 2026, nine cafés</div><div class="val">{{ t.chk_g | pct }} <span style="font-size:15px;color:var(--g700)">checks</span></div><div class="cap">Average check {{ t.tkt_g | pct }}. The budget is volume only; volume alone grew {{ t.chk_g | apct(0) }} this year.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 10 GAP #}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>Five cafés carry {{ "%.0f" | format(n.strong.share * 100) }}% of the {{ t.gap | fm(1) }} gap between the budget and our plan</h1>
  <p class="lede">Our plan is the blend of three forecasting models, shaded down because over-forecasting costs us more than under-forecasting. For {{ n.below_low | length }} of the nine, the budget is below even our most cautious model. For three ({{ n.suggest.kept | join(", ") }}) we still think the budget's number is fair.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <div class="chart-title">Our 2027 plan minus the budget, by café</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Pink: objective too low · light pink: slightly low · gray: defensible or in line</div>
      {{ svg.gaps }}
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.25">
      <table class="roomy">
        <thead><tr><th class="l">Café</th><th>Budget<br>2027</th><th>Our plan<br>2027</th><th>Our three<br>models</th><th class="l">Our read</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for s in n.nine %}{% set c = C[s] %}
          <tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ c.b27 | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ c.plan27 | fm }}</b></td><td class="dim">{{ c.low27 | frange(c.high27) }}</td><td class="l">{{ badge(c.verdict) }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Nine existing cafés</td><td>{{ t.b27 | fm }}</td><td class="pink">{{ t.plan27 | fm }}</td><td>{{ t.low27 | frange(t.high27) }}</td><td class="l">{{ t.gap | sfm }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot("Our three models: Prophet, SARIMA and Holt-Winters, fitted café by café through Sep 2026 · plan = blend × " ~ ("%.3f" | format(n.plan_cfg.factor))) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 11 BOLDER #}
{% set O = n.openings %}{% set cv = C["La Jolla Cove"] %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>Where the budget is bolder than we are: new cafés and the Cove remodel</h1>
  <p class="lede">Our models cannot see openings or remodels, so we check these lines against our own track record. Both lean high, and both are worth budgeting more cautiously.</p>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.35">
      <h3>New cafés: budget against our last four openings</h3>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th class="l">Opening</th><th>First 8<br>months</th><th>First 10<br>months</th><th>First 12<br>months</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for a in O.analogs %}
          <tr><td>{{ a.store }} <span class="dim">({{ a.opened.strftime("%b %Y") }})</span></td><td>{{ a[8] | fm }}</td><td>{{ a[10] | fm }}</td><td>{{ a[12] | fm }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Average opening</td><td>{{ O.avg[8] | fm }}</td><td>{{ O.avg[10] | fm }}</td><td>{{ O.avg[12] | fm }}</td></tr>
        {% for x in O.new %}
          <tr class="{{ 'sep' if loop.first else '' }}"><td class="pink">Budget: {{ x.name }} <span class="dim">(opens {{ x.opens.strftime("%b %-d") }}, {{ x.months }} months)</span></td>
            <td>{{ (x.budget | fm) if x.months == 8 else "" }}</td><td>{{ (x.budget | fm) if x.months == 10 else "" }}</td><td class="dim">{{ x.first12 | replace(" first 12 months", "") }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% set nb = n.bridge27.new_budget %}{% set best = O.new | sum(attribute="best") %}{% set la = O.new | sum(attribute="la") %}
      <h3 style="margin-top:16px">Both openings in 2027</h3>
      <div class="ledger compact">
        <div class="r"><div class="what">Budget</div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ nb / best * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ nb | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">If both open like {{ O.best_name }}, our best</div><div><div class="bar" style="width:100%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ best | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">If both open like our average opening</div><div><div class="bar ours" style="width:{{ n.bridge27.new_track / best * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt pink">{{ n.bridge27.new_track | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">If both open like our LA openings</div><div><div class="bar" style="width:{{ la / best * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ la | fm }}</div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:6px">Budget ramps: {% for x in O.new %}{{ x.name }} {{ x.first_month | fk }} in its first month, peaking at {{ x.peak | fk }} in {{ x.peak_month }}{{ "; " if not loop.last else ". " }}{% endfor %}Openings restated at 2026 prices (average check up {{ "%.0f" | format(O.check_lift_23 * 100) }}% since 2023 and {{ "%.0f" | format(O.check_lift_24 * 100) }}% since 2024). {{ O.tbd | join(", ") }} has no volume in the budget and none here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <h3>La Jolla Cove remodel</h3>
      <div class="minis" style="margin-bottom:12px">
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Average month, 2026</div><div class="val">{{ cv.avg_m | fk }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Best month ever</div><div class="val">{{ cv.best_m | fk }}</div><div class="sub">{{ cv.best_m_label }}</div></div>
        <div class="m"><div class="lab">Budget, Oct–Dec 2027</div><div class="val pink">$125K</div><div class="sub">a month</div></div>
      </div>
      <table class="roomy" style="margin-bottom:12px">
        <thead><tr><th class="l">La Jolla Cove, 2027</th><th>Budget</th><th>Current trend</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>January–September</td><td>{{ cv.b_js | fm }}</td><td>{{ cv.p_js | fm }}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>October–December</td><td class="pink">{{ cv.b_q4 | fm }}</td><td>{{ cv.p_q4 | fm }}</td></tr>
          <tr class="total"><td>Year</td><td>{{ cv.b27 | fm }}</td><td>{{ cv.plan27 | fm }}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p style="font-size:12.5px;margin:0 0 10px">The hotel around the Cove has been under remodel since March 2026, so the café is open but soft. The budget holds January–September flat to 2026, close to our view; the difference is October–December, after the October 1, 2027 reopening: a $1.5M annual rate, {{ "%.1f" | format(cv.ratio) }}× today's monthly sales.</p>
      <p style="font-size:12.5px;margin:0">No café of ours has a remodel in its history, so we cannot test the lift. We would budget the trend and add the lift once the Cove reopens and trades.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot("Openings measured from the first trading day · new-café months open in 2027 per the budget") }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 12 TOTAL COMPANY #}
{% set Z = n.bridge27 %}{% set zmax = Z.ours %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>Total company: {{ Z.ours | fm(1) }} in our plan against {{ Z.budget | fm(1) }} in the budget</h1>
  <p class="lede">The existing cafés and Nautilus add {{ (Z.existing + Z.nautilus) | fm(1) }}; a more cautious view of the Cove remodel and the two openings takes back {{ (-(Z.cove + Z.new)) | fm(1) }}. Net, the budget is {{ (Z.ours - Z.budget) | fm(1) }} below our plan.</p>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.5">
      <div class="ledger">
        <div class="r"><div class="what">Budget 2027: total company<small>nine cafés, Cove, Manhattan Beach, Sportsmen's Lodge</small></div><div><div class="bar base" style="width:{{ Z.budget / zmax * 100 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ Z.budget | fm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ Nine existing cafés at our plan<small>{{ t.plan27 | fm }} against {{ t.b27 | fm }}</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ Z.existing / zmax * 100 * 4 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt pink">{{ Z.existing | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">+ Nautilus<small>not in the budget</small></div><div><div class="bar plus" style="width:{{ Z.nautilus / zmax * 100 * 4 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt pink">{{ Z.nautilus | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">− La Jolla Cove on its current trend<small>remodel lift left out until it trades</small></div><div><div class="bar minus" style="width:{{ -Z.cove / zmax * 100 * 4 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ Z.cove | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r"><div class="what">− New cafés at our average opening<small>{{ Z.new_track | fm }} against {{ Z.new_budget | fm }}</small></div><div><div class="bar minus" style="width:{{ -Z.new / zmax * 100 * 4 }}%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ Z.new | sfm }}</div></div>
        <div class="r tot final"><div class="what">= Our plan 2027: total company</div><div><div class="bar ours" style="width:100%"></div></div><div class="amt">{{ Z.ours | fm }}</div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px">Adjustment bars at 4× scale. Boulangerie (opens April) has no volume in the budget or here. Growth on 2026: budget {{ (Z.budget / n.budget_total26 - 1) | pct }}, our plan {{ (Z.ours / n.all26 - 1) | pct }} (on each one's 2026 total).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <h3>Risks to our plan</h3>
      <ul class="tight big">
        <li><b>Brentwood has gone flat.</b> Sales have held near {{ C["Brentwood"].avg_m | fk }} a month since January; if that continues, our plan is about {{ C["Brentwood"].gap | fk }} high there.</li>
        <li><b>Coronado is cooling.</b> Growth fell from {{ C["Coronado"].q1 | pct(0) }} in Q1 to {{ C["Coronado"].oct_g | pct(0) }} in October; our lowest model puts it at {{ C["Coronado"].low27 | fm }}.</li>
        <li><b>Competitors next door.</b> The budget expects them at Del Mar and Brentwood. Our models cannot see them; we would carry them as explicit risk lines.</li>
        <li><b>A broad slowdown</b> would hit every café at once. Our plan already assumes growth eases from {{ t.g26 | apct(0) }} to {{ t.pg | apct(0) }}.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 13 WHAT WE SUGGEST #}
{% set S = n.suggest %}
<section class="page">
  {{ head("Part 2 · 2027") }}
  <h1>What we suggest: {{ S.total | fm }} for 2027, {{ S.total_change | sfm }} above the budget</h1>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6px">
    <div class="col" style="flex:1.7">
      <table class="roomy">
        <thead><tr><th class="l">Café or line</th><th>Budget 2027</th><th>Suggested</th><th>Change</th><th class="l">Basis</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for s in n.nine %}{% set c = C[s] %}
          <tr><td>{{ c.name }}</td><td>{{ c.b27 | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ c.suggest | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (c.suggest - c.b27) | sfk if (c.suggest - c.b27) | abs > 1 else "—" }}</td>
            <td class="l">{% if c.verdict in ["defensible", "in_line"] %}<span class="dim">Keep the budget ({{ VERDICT_LABEL[c.verdict] | lower }})</span>{% else %}Our plan{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Nine existing cafés</td><td>{{ t.b27 | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.nine | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.nine_change | sfm }}</td><td class="l">{{ (S.nine / t.e26 - 1) | pct }} on 2026</td></tr>
          <tr class="sep"><td>Nautilus</td><td class="dim">—</td><td><b>{{ C["Nautilus"].plan27 | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ C["Nautilus"].plan27 | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Our plan; not in the budget</td></tr>
          <tr><td>La Jolla Cove</td><td>{{ cv.b27 | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ cv.plan27 | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (cv.plan27 - cv.b27) | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Current trend; add the remodel lift once it trades</td></tr>
          {% for x in O.new %}
          <tr><td>{{ x.name }}</td><td>{{ x.budget | fm }}</td><td><b>{{ x.track | fm }}</b></td><td>{{ (x.track - x.budget) | sfk }}</td><td class="l">Our average opening, {{ x.months }} months</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
          <tr class="total"><td>Total company</td><td>{{ S.total_budget | fm }}</td><td class="pink">{{ S.total | fm }}</td><td>{{ S.total_change | sfm }}</td><td class="l">{{ S.total_g | pct }} on 2026</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="col" style="flex:1">
      <h3>How we got there</h3>
      <ul class="tight big">
        <li><b>Raise six objectives</b> to our plan: {{ S.raised | join(", ") }}.</li>
        <li><b>Keep three</b> where the budget's caution has support: {{ S.kept | join(", ") }}.</li>
        <li><b>Show judgment calls as their own lines</b>: competitors next door, the Cove remodel and openings beyond our track record are upside or risk, not the base.</li>
        <li><b>Re-forecast every month</b> as actuals land; the models update themselves.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="callout" style="margin-top:14px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:12px">Even the suggested {{ S.nine | fm }} for the nine cafés assumes growth slows from {{ t.g26 | apct(0) }} to {{ (S.nine / t.e26 - 1) | apct(0) }}.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{ foot(SRC) }}
</section>

{# ================================================================== 14 DIVIDER 3 + INDEX #}
<section class="page divider">
  <div class="div-left" style="padding-right:.5in">
    <div class="part">Part 3</div>
    <div class="div-title" style="font-size:44px">Café by café</div>
    <p class="div-sub" style="margin-bottom:16px">Two pages each: the numbers, then the evidence behind our read.</p>
    <table style="font-size:11.5px">
      <thead><tr><th class="l">Café</th><th>Budget</th><th>Our plan</th><th class="l">Our read</th><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
